    {
      "kind": "javascript-module",
      "path": "packages/interactions/core/src/elements/qti-gap/qti-gap.ts",
      "declarations": [
        {
          "kind": "class",
          "name": "QtiGap",
          "tagName": "qti-gap",
          "description": "A gap in the prose, and the first drop target to render its own chips.\n\nThe interaction owns placement and publishes it on `dragDropContext`; this element subscribes and\nrenders what it holds. Nothing appends into it. That inverts the old flow, where `handleDrop` did\n`cloneNode` + `appendChild` and the response was recovered afterwards by reading the DOM back\nout — which is why placement and the response could ever disagree at all.\n\nThe chips land in this shadow root rather than in the light DOM, so a theme reaches them as\n`::part(drag)` — a bare `::part()` matches in any shadow root — instead of by tag. The gap's own\n`:state(filled)` says whether it holds anything.",
          "attributes": [
            {
              "name": "identifier",
              "type": {
                "text": "string"
              },
              "fieldName": "identifier"
            },
            {
              "name": "tabindex",
              "type": {
                "text": "number | undefined"
              },
              "default": "0",
              "fieldName": "tabindex"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "exports": []
    },
